# =============================================================
#  Portfolio client - environment variables
#  Copy to `.env` and adjust. Only VITE_-prefixed values are exposed
#  to the browser bundle, so never put a secret in this file.
# =============================================================

# ---- API base URL -------------------------------------------
# LEAVE THIS UNSET during local development.
#
# When it is unset the app calls relative paths ("/api/projects") and the Vite
# dev server proxies them to http://localhost:4000. That means no hardcoded
# localhost URL in the code and no CORS preflights while developing.
#
# Set it when the frontend and backend are hosted separately, e.g.
# VITE_API_URL=https://portfolio-api.onrender.com
#
# VITE_API_URL=

# ---- Deploying to Vercel ------------------------------------
# On Vercel the frontend and the API are separate projects, so this MUST be set
# to the API's deployed URL. Add it in the Vercel dashboard under
# Settings -> Environment Variables, then redeploy - Vite inlines VITE_ values
# at BUILD time, so changing it later requires a new deployment, not just a
# restart.
#
#   VITE_API_URL=https://your-api-project.vercel.app
#
# No trailing slash, and no /api suffix - the app appends that itself.
#
# Setting this also means the browser calls the API cross-origin, so the API's
# CLIENT_URL must list this frontend's origin or CORS will block every request.
